                  \\,.
          %p
            (On the left is the image under forming
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectra"} Thom spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+rings"} cobordism rings
            of the first stages in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+tower"} Whitehead tower
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi BO
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BO
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+spin+structure"} higher spin structure
          %p
            Observe here that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+modular+forms"} topological modular forms
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficient"} coefficient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            known as
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genera"} genera
            (see there) tend to appear as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorifications"} decategorifications
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
            out of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of a homomorphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi M
                  %mi String
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sigma \colon M String \longrightarrow tmf
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+bordism"} String bordism
            to the
            = succeed "-spectrum." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation
            in universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            indeed exists and is called the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-orientation"} sigma-orientation
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+orientation+of+tmf"} string orientation of tmf
          %p
            This construction has been the central motivation behind the search for and construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hopkins94"}> Hopkins 94
            ). A construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+orientation+of+tmf"} string orientation of tmf
            is given in (
            %a{:href => "#AndoHopkinsRezk"}> Ando-Hopkins-Rezk 10
            ) and it is shown that indeed it refines the Witten genus (
            %a{:href => "#AndoHopkinsRezk"}> Ando-Hopkins-Rezk 10, prop. 15.3
            ).
          %p
            It is maybe noteworthy that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            (and hence its universal string orientation) also arises canonically from just studying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+homotopy+theory"} chromatic homotopy theory
            (see
            %a{:href => "#tmf#MazelGee13"} Mazel-Gee 13
            for a nice survey of this) a fundamental topic in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"}> string theory
            ).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#CharacteristicSeries Characteristic series
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "genus#LogarithmAndCharacteristicSeries"} characteristic series
            of the Witten genus as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"} power series
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in formal power series in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi K
                            %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mfrac
                            %mi z
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi exp
                                %mi w
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi q
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mfrac
                            %mi z
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi σ
                                %mi L
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi q
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mn 2
                            %mrow
                              %mi sinh
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo ≥
                              %mn 1
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %msup
                                %mi q
                                %mi n
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mn 2
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %msup
                                %mi q
                                %mi n
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %msup
                                %mi q
                                %mi n
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi exp
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo ≥
                                %mn 2
                            %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mi G
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi z
                                  %mi k
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo !
                            %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  K_w(z)(q)
                  \&amp; =
                  \\frac{z}{\exp_w(z)(q)}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  \\frac{z}{\sigma_L(z)(q)}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  \\frac{z/2}{sinh(z/2)}
                  \\prod_{n \geq 1}
                  \\frac{(1-q^n)^2}{(1-q^n e^z)(1-q^n e^{-z})}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  \\exp\left(
                  \\sum_{k \geq 2} 2G_k(q) \frac{z^k}{k!}
                  \\right)
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,,
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_L
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weierstrass+sigma-function"} Weierstrass sigma-function
                (see e.g.
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a{:href => "#AndoBasterra00"} Ando Basterra 00, section 5.1
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_k
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eisenstein+series"} Eisenstein series
                (
                %a{:href => "#Zagier86"}> Zagier 86, equation (14)
                ,
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#AndoHopkinsRezk10"} Ando-Hopkins-Rezk 10, prop. 10.9
          %p
            This is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+form"} modular form
            with respect to the variable
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            %em
              %a{:href => "#IntegralityAndModularity"} Integrality and modularity
            \. Such functions which are power series of two variables
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            with elliptic nature in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            and modular nature in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            are called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+forms"} Jacobi forms
            (
            %a{:href => "#Zagier86"}> Zagier 86, p. 8
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AndoFrenchGanter08"} Ando-French-Ganter 08
          %p
            There are various further ways to equivalently re-express the above in terms of other special
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+forms"} modular forms
          %h4#CharacteristicSeriesInTermsOfKacWeylCharacters In terms of Kac-Weyl characters
          %p
            The Witten genus has a close relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kac-Weyl+character"} Kac-Weyl character
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+group+representations"} loop group representations
          %p
            Consider of four
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible
            = succeed "-1" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level"} level
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin+group"} Spin
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2k)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+group+representation"} loop group representation
            the one denoted
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo −
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Rep
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tilde S_+ - \tilde S_- \in Rep(\tilde L Spin(2k))
          %p
            and write its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kac-Weyl+character"} Kac-Weyl character
            as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Rep
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 12
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\chi(\tilde S_+ - \tilde S_-) \in Rep(Spin(2k))[ [ q^{1/12} ] ]
                  \\,.
          %p
            Under passing to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+characters"} group characters
            this is (
            %a{:href => "#Brylinski90"}> Brylinski 90, p. 7(467)
            , reviewed in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#KL96"} KL 96, section 1.2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %munderover
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mn 1
                        %mi k
                      %mi θ
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi η
                        %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\chi(\tilde S_+ - \tilde S_-) = \frac{\prod_{1}^k \theta}{\eta^k}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where on the right we have the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+theta-function"} Jacobi theta-function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            divided by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+eta-function"} Dedekind eta-function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
          %p
            Comparison shows that in terms of this the exponential series of the Witten genus is equivalently (by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/splitting+principle"} splitting principle
            the
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi exp
                    %mi w
                  %mo =
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi w
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi η
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp_w = z/K_w = \eta^2 \, \chi(\tilde S_+ - \tilde S_-)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice that, by the relation (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "equivariant+elliptic+cohomology#RelationToLoopGroupRepresentations"} here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+group+representations"} loop group representations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(\tilde S_+ - \tilde S_-)
            may be regarded as an element of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(2k)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            of the point (at the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tate+curve"} Tate curve
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+ad-equivariant+Tate+K-theory"} twisted ad-equivariant Tate K-theory
          %h3#IntegralityAndModularity Integrality and modularity
          %p
            A priori, the Witten genus has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"} power series
            ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}[ [q] ]
            over the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly+cancellation"} quantum anomaly cancellation
          %h4#ModularityForTypeIISuperstring For the type II superstring
          %p
            The genus obtained from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring"} type II superstring
            in the NS-R sector is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+form"} modular form
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence+subgroup"} congruence subgroup
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_2(2)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Witten87a"} Witten 87a, below (13)
            %em
              %a{:href => "level+structure+on+an+elliptic+curve#RelationToSpinStructures"} congruence subgroup – Relation to spin structures
            for more.
          %p
            Hence, with suitable normalization, the universal Witten-Ochanine genus takes values in the subring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi MF
                    %mo •
                    %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MF_\bullet^{\mathbb{Q}}(\Gamma_0(2)) \hookrightarrow \mathbb{Q}[ [q] ]
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+forms"} modular forms
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msub
                    %mi SL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_0(2)\subset SL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            with rational coefficients (
            %a{:href => "#Zagier86"} Zagier 86, item d) on page 2
            based on
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ChudnovskyChudnovsky88"} Chudnovsky-Chudnovsky 88
          %h4#ModularityForHeteroticString For the heterotic superstring
          %p
            On manifolds with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            the heterotic string Witten genus has integral coeffcients, hence in the ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[ [ q ] ]
            (
            %a{:href => "#ChudnovskyChudnovsky88"}> Chudnovsky-Chudnovsky 88
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Landweber88"} Landweber 88
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KreckStolz93"} Kreck-Stolz 93
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Hovey91"} Hovey 91
          %p
            On manifolds with rational
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            (meaning spin structure and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+fractional+Pontryagin+class"} first fractional Pontryagin class
            is at most
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+forms"} modular forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi MF
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MF_\bullet
            (
            %a{:href => "#Zagier86"}> Zagier 86, page 6
            ).
          %p
            On manifolds with actual
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+modular+forms"} topological modular forms
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hopkins94"}> Hopkins 94
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AndoHopkinsRezk"} Ando-Hopkins-Rezk 10
          %h3#RelationToSuSyQMOnLoopSpace Relation to Dirac operators and supersymmetric QM on loop space
          %p
            Originally in (
            %a{:href => "#Witten87a"}> Witten 87a
            ) the elliptic genus was derived as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+volume+limit"} large volume limit
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} index
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercharge"} supercharge
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Witten87b"} Witten87b
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac-Ramond+operator"} Dirac-Ramond operator
            – would really behave like a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator+on+smooth+loop+space"} Dirac operator on smooth loop space
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+of+a+Dirac+operator"} index of a Dirac operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            acts by rigid rotationl of the parameterization of the loops, and by analogy standard formulas for equivariant indices in K-theory would imply the localization to the tangent spaces to the space of constant loops.
          %p
            Notice that the would-be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator+on+smooth+loop+space"} Dirac operator on smooth loop space
            is what would realize the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            quantum dynamics as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric+quantum+mechanics"} supersymmetric quantum mechanics
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+loop+space"} smooth loop space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric+quantum+mechanics"} supersymmetric quantum mechanics
            in (
            %a{:href => "#Witten82"}> Witten 82
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Witten85"} Witten 85
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+vector+field"} Killing vector field
            (correspinding to the
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
          %h3#TwistedWittenGenus Heterotic (twisted) Witten genus, loop group representations and parameterized WZW models
          %p
            If the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            in question is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            then generally there is a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+string-structure"}> twist
            ” of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+fields"} background fields
            by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            some simply connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
            (notably
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"} E8
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Witten87"} Witten 87, equations (30), (31)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Brylinski90"} Brylinski 90
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#KL95"} KL 95
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+string+structure"} twisted string structure
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string%5Ec+2-group"} String^c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+Chern+class"} second Chern class
            (explicitly identified as such in (
            %a{:href => "#ChenHanZhang10"}> Chen-Han-Zhang 10
            ).
          %p
            An elegant formulation of twisted Witten genera (and proof of their rigidity) in terms of highest weight
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+group+representations"} loop group representations
            is given in (
            %a{:href => "#KL95"}> KL 95
            ) along the lines of (
            %a{:href => "#Brylinski90"}> Brylinski 90
            ). In (
            %a{:href => "#DistlerSharpe07"}> Distler-Sharpe 07
            ), following suggestions around (
            %a{:href => "#Ando07"}> Ando 07
            ) this is interpreted geometrically in terms of fiberwise
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} indices
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+WZW+models"} parameterized WZW models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            to the given
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} String
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
          %p
            What should be a concrete computation of the twisted Witten genus specifically for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"} E8
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#Harris12"}> Harris 12, section 4
            ).
          %h3#as_the_global_character_of_sheaves_of_vertex_operator_algebras As the global character of sheaves of vertex operator algebras
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset \mathbb{C}
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
            then the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mi ch
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}^{ch}(U)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+differential+operators"} chiral differential operators
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is naturally a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vertex+operator+algebra"} super vertex operator algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            such that its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+Chern+class"} second Chern class
            vanish over the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+of+vertex+operator+algebras"} sheaf of vertex operator algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mi X
                    %mi ch
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}^{ch}_X(-)
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mi X
                    %mi ch
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^\bullet(\mathcal{D}^{ch}_X)
            is itself a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vertex+operator+algebra"} super vertex operator algebra
            and its super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kac-Weyl+character"} Kac-Weyl character
            is proportional to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w(X)
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi char
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mi X
                    %mi ch
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∝
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  char H^\bullet(\mathcal{D}^{ch}_X)\propto w(X)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Physically this result is understood by observing that
            = succeed "is" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mi X
                      %mi ch
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}^{ch}_X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+observables"} quantum observables
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+twist"} topologically twisted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 2d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
            (see there for more on this) of which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            is (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+volume+limit"} large volume limit
            of) the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
          %p
            As highlighted in (
            %a{:href => "#Cheung10"}> Cheung 10, p. 2
            ), there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+Dolbeault+complex"} chiral Dolbeault complex
            which gives a precise sense in which over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            the Witten genus is a stringy analog of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+genus"} Todd genus
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Cheung10"} Cheung 10
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves+of+vertex+operator+algebras"} sheaves of vertex operator algebras
            over more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            manifolds is addressed.
          %h3#stolz_conjecture Stolz conjecture
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stolz+conjecture"} Stolz conjecture
            due to (
            %a{:href => "#Stolz96"}> Stolz 96
            ) asserts that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed manifold
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+structure"} String structure
            which furthermore admits a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ricci+curvature"} Ricci curvature
          %h3#RelationToBPSStateCounting Relation to BPS state counting on target space
          %p
            By
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            and by the same argument that controls the expression of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+of+a+Dirac+operator"} index of a Dirac operator
            in terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric+quantum+mechanics"} supersymmetric quantum mechanics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercharge"} supercharge
            acts trivially. In terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            theory these are the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+states"} BPS states
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Dijkgraaf98"} Dijkgraaf 98
          %p
            Therefore the Witten genus may also be used as a generating function for BPS state counting. As such it has for instance been used in the microscopic explanation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bekenstein-Hawking+entropy"} Bekenstein-Hawking entropy
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes"} black holes
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes+in+string+theory"} black holes in string theory
          %h3#relation_to_cayley_plane_bundles Relation to Cayley plane bundles
